The [link asio.reference.deferred_t `deferred_t`] class is used to indicate that an asynchronous operation should return a function object which is itself an initiation function. A [link asio.reference.deferred_t `deferred_t`] object may be passed as a completion token to an asynchronous operation, typically using the special value `asio::deferred`. For example:



   auto my_deferred_op
     = my_socket.async_read_some(my_buffer,
         asio::deferred); 




The initiating function (async\_read\_some in the above example) returns a function object that will lazily initiate the operation. 

