The thread pool class is an execution context where functions are permitted to run on one of a fixed number of threads.


[heading Submitting tasks to the pool]
  


To submit functions to the thread pool, use the [link asio.reference.dispatch `dispatch`], [link asio.reference.post `post`] or [link asio.reference.defer `defer`] free functions.

For example:



   void my_task()
   {
     ...
   }

   ...

   // Launch the pool with four threads.
   asio::thread_pool pool(4);

   // Submit a function to the pool.
   asio::post(pool, my_task);

   // Submit a lambda object to the pool.
   asio::post(pool,
       []()
       {
         ...
       });

   // Wait for all tasks in the pool to complete.
   pool.join(); 




