The [link asio.reference.use_future_t `use_future_t`] class is a completion token type that is used to indicate that an asynchronous operation should return a std::future object. A [link asio.reference.use_future_t `use_future_t`] object may be passed as a completion token to an asynchronous operation, typically using the special value `asio::use_future`. For example:



   std::future<std::size_t> my_future
     = my_socket.async_read_some(my_buffer, asio::use_future); 




The initiating function (async\_read\_some in the above example) returns a future that will receive the result of the operation. If the operation completes with an [link asio.reference.error_code `error_code`] indicating failure, it is converted into a [link asio.reference.system_error `system_error`] and passed back to the caller via the future. 

