The [link asio.reference.basic_yield_context `basic_yield_context`] class is a completion token type that is used to represent the currently executing stackful coroutine. A [link asio.reference.basic_yield_context `basic_yield_context`] object may be passed as a completion token to an asynchronous operation. For example:



   template <typename Executor>
   void my_coroutine(basic_yield_context<Executor> yield)
   {
     ...
     std::size_t n = my_socket.async_read_some(buffer, yield);
     ...
   } 




The initiating function (async\_read\_some in the above example) suspends the current coroutine. The coroutine is resumed when the asynchronous operation completes, and the result of the operation is returned. 


